{"id":"000VWH","title":"The Little Robot's Crayon","author":"Kainapple","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-07T10:22:39+00:00","posted":"Heute, 05:00 Uhr","rules":"Rules:\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nAn X joins digits that sum to 10.\n\nA white dot joins consecutive digits.\n\nA black dot joins digits where one is double the other.\n\nA robot is moving around the grid in a loop, and it's just a baby, it hasn't learned left turns yet.\n\nThe robot does the following:\n\n• Checks the digit it's standing on,\n\n• Moves that many cells forward,\n\n• Turns 90° clockwise (on the spot),\n\n• Repeat.\n\nYou can see the robot currently moving east in row 8.\n\nThe robot shades in any dots it walks directly over, meaning they function as black dots instead of white dots.\n\nThe robot never walks directly over an X.\n\nThe digits the robot checks are all small enough to keep it in the grid.\n\nThe robot may re-enter a cell during the loop only if it never turns in that cell. As such, sudokupads's pen tool can be used to show the loop unambiguously.\n\nSudokuPad link\nEnjoy!","solutionCode":"Digits in row 2 that are unvisited by the robot, from left to right.","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki","XV (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/yhtmrmdawy","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/yhtmrmdawy","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-07T10:22:39+00:00"}